Aider v0.36.1-dev
Models: gpt-4o with diff edit format, weak model gpt-3.5-turbo

### Issue

To reproduce, run `aider --show-repo-map` on the following files.
`hello.js`:
```js
/**
 * Example doc comment
 */
function f() {
  f();
}
```
`hello.rs`:
```rust
/// Example doc comment
fn f() {
    f();
}
```

Aider produces this repomap:
```
hello.js:
⋮...
│function f() {
│  f();
⋮...

hello.rs:
⋮...
│fn f() {
│    f();
⋮...
```

I haven't done any experiments, but intuitively, it seems it would be beneficial to include (possibly truncated) doc comments to the repo map. There are probably more valuable that the first few lines of the function body (except for Python where doc comments are part of the function body).

